messages:
anne: Quick heads-up — seeing inconsistent embedding dims when paginating rerank inputs from the Go client. Some pages 1536, others 1024. stack trace below, unsure if SDK, runtime router, or our paginator.

mike: ouch. can you share a minimal request/response sample? which model id are you calling?

anne: calling `text-embed-3-large` (should be 1536). sample logs: embeddings[0].len=1536 then later embeddings[2].len=1024. we don't touch vectors between paginator -> batcher.

lina: two likely causes i've hit: 1) mixing responses from different model variants (old 1024 -> new 1536) due to a router fallback; 2) batcher incorrectly padding/truncating when merging pages.

eugene: also double-check the Go SDK streaming code path — there was a bug where streaming chunks used a stale model-metadata cache, so mid-stream fallback produced a different dim. if the batcher blindly concatenates you'll get silent bad vectors.

anne: repro (Go):
```
// simplified
pages := paginator.FetchAll(ctx)
for _, p := range pages {
  for _, e := range p.Embeddings {
    log.Printf("got dim=%d", len(e.Vector))
  }
  batcher.AddPage(p)
}
out := batcher.Flush()
```

sam: which client version? can you attach a raw page payload (sanitized) with the 1024 vectors?

anne: client v0.24.1. attached two page payloads in the ticket: pageA (1536) and pageB (1024). both look like normal model responses; top-level "model" field sometimes absent and some chunks lack a "model_id" header.

lina: that missing "model_id" matches a past issue — older streaming chunks didn't include explicit model id, and our router relies on the first chunk to set the cache. if a fallback occurs later the cache isn't updated and dims mix.

mike: short-term mitigation: validate dims before merge and return a clear error, e.g. throw ErrDimMismatch with details. long-term: fix streaming metadata cache and add unit/e2e tests that simulate mid-stream fallback.

anne: i'll add the validation to the Go batcher and fail fast so callers can log and surface the error. opening a PR now.

embed-ci-bot: new ticket created: INF-1298 "embed-batcher: validate embedding dims on page merge" assigned to anne.

eugene: also add dedupe-by-id inside the paginator — retries produced duplicate vectors which confused rerank that expects unique ids. small but noisy for debugging.

sam: +1 on dedupe. can we make the error message suggest the likely causes (model mismatch vs router fallback) so customers have actionable next steps?

anne: plan: 1) quick patch in Go SDK batcher to validate dims + dedupe (PR in ~2h), 2) add unit/e2e test simulating streaming chunks that swap model id mid-stream, 3) follow-up infra change to ensure every chunk includes a `model_id` header. i'll ping reviewers.

mike: ping @lina @eugene for reviews. also please add tiny repro scripts (py + go) so oncall can reproduce locally/ci.

anne: pseudo validation i'm adding:
```
func mergePages(pages []Page) ([]Embedding, error) {
  var expectedDim int
  for i, p := range pages {
    for _, e := range p.Embeddings {
      if i == 0 && expectedDim == 0 { expectedDim = len(e.Vector) }
      if len(e.Vector) != expectedDim {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("dim mismatch: expected=%d got=%d on page=%d", expectedDim, len(e.Vector), i)
      }
    }
  }
  // dedupe by id, then concat
  return merged, nil
}
```

lina: looks good. add a telemetry counter `dim_mismatch` with context (model_header_present, model_id_value) so we can triage server vs client. :eyes: 

anne: added telemetry to the WIP. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-go/pull/681 (WIP) — tagging reviewers.

mike: i'll review after lunch. if it's small we can cut a hotfix for Dedicated customers affected. :thumbsup: 

anne: thanks — i'll post updates in the PR and ping infra about the chunk header fix.

embed-ci-bot: CI started for PR #681 (go-sdk-tests).
